<title>USA: L.A. County board approves probation camp funding.</title>
<headline>L.A. County board approves probation camp funding.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Los Angeles County Board of Supervisors voted on Thursday to use the county's operating reserve and other funds to keep probation camps open, the county's spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Supervisors agreed to shift funds to secure the $48.5 million needed to keep the camps from closing, spokeswoman Judy Hammond said.</p>
<p>The board also voted to approve contracts that would allow the county to open the Twin Towers jail, Hammond said.</p>
